dback","hacktoberfest","open-source","rails","ruby"],"visibility":"public","forks":4153,"open_issues":555,"watchers":22543,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\r\n\r\nSomewhat related to #708. Since all saved posts are not shown on the Reading List (just 45, which I assume is for performance), it doesn't make sense to show the list of tags for the entire reading list. The pain point here is that clicking `#career (60)` might only show 10 things since only 10 of the most recent 45 are tagged with career. Or worse, clicking `#portfolio (2)` will say there is nothing in the reading list to display.\r\n\r\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\r\n\r\nIf 45 max are to be displayed at any given time, I would expect the tags list to only show the tags relevant to the 45 items I can see. Also, the counts should reflect the count within the available items not the entire reading list.\r\n\r\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\r\n\r\nIf #708 gets addressed, this is moot. Also, depending on why the 45 is how it is, it may be a nice alternative to have selecting the tag to requery the reading list and pull all the relevant ones under that tag. Like in the above example, `#portfolio (2)` has none originally but specifying that I want to read those ones makes it shown.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\n![screen shot 2018-10-26 at 7 07 32 pm](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11020425/47596196-abf05480-d952-11e8-89d1-e572eedb5bcb.png)\r\nA screenshot of the tags I'm talking about since the Reading List doesn't get much love so people may not be aware of the tags.\r\n\r\nIt's nice to see the tags I clearly want to read later, but the act of clicking them is utterly useless in its current state since it only filters the most recent articles.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/forem/forem/issues/1015/re